WEBVTT

00:04.700 --> 00:07.910
<i>"You mustn't use thymia to hurt another."</i>

00:08.580 --> 00:12.400
<i>Thus were the children of the Mud Whale taught and raised.</i>

00:13.990 --> 00:17.450
<i>In spite of this, we resolved ourselves to fight.</i>

00:19.050 --> 00:24.770
<i>The training we engaged in to prepare ourselves for the Imperial battleship Skylos' attack </i>

00:24.770 --> 00:27.230
<i>was little more than child's play.</i>

00:28.540 --> 00:33.470
<i>Even so, we devoted ourselves to it seriously.</i>

00:35.330 --> 00:38.700
<i>Thymia cannot be used directly on people.</i>

00:39.330 --> 00:44.640
<i>When we use our powers, they must be focused on bows and arrows or bladed weaponry. </i>

00:46.840 --> 00:51.150
That's it. Imagine the shape of the bow in your head.

00:51.150 --> 00:55.000
Picture it bending back, and don't forget the arrow.

00:55.000 --> 00:56.030
I won't fowget!

00:56.950 --> 01:00.320
Pull back the string and look straight at your target.

01:00.320 --> 01:00.910
Wook at it.

01:01.240 --> 01:02.920
See the arrow piercing it.

01:02.920 --> 01:04.030
Piersh!

01:06.350 --> 01:11.830
<i>The children can draw bows beyond their strength with the help of thymia.</i>

01:12.350 --> 01:14.380
<i>It increases their accuracy as well.</i>

01:14.950 --> 01:19.430
<i>We were already accustomed to the basic use of moving objects with thymia.</i>

01:20.670 --> 01:21.970
Hey, you.

01:22.400 --> 01:24.680
Come with us.

01:24.680 --> 01:25.840
What do you even—

01:25.840 --> 01:27.150
Shut up, you.

01:27.150 --> 01:28.720
Dork.

01:28.720 --> 01:30.150
Bald dork.

01:30.840 --> 01:32.830
Archiving destroyer dork.

01:33.800 --> 01:34.900
Let's go.

01:41.030 --> 01:42.950
Are you guys okay?

01:46.520 --> 01:47.830
What do you want?

01:50.920 --> 01:51.630
Take them out.

01:57.810 --> 01:59.930
Your clothes are all torn up.

01:59.930 --> 02:02.930
We felt sorry for you, so Shinono suggested we get you new ones.

02:03.290 --> 02:05.560
I think this color would look great with your skin.

02:05.560 --> 02:07.020
This one's cute too!

02:07.020 --> 02:08.160
That's great!

02:08.160 --> 02:10.020
<i>I can't fight in these.</i>

02:10.680 --> 02:13.180
Do you mind if I modify them to move more easily in?

02:13.180 --> 02:16.070
Go ahead. I'll lend you my sewing set.

02:16.630 --> 02:19.100
I'm Urumi. Let's be friends.

02:19.100 --> 02:23.850
You should hang with us instead of sticking around those boring guys.

02:23.850 --> 02:25.150
Right?

02:25.150 --> 02:28.770
We're all pretty confident in our thymia.

02:30.960 --> 02:33.170
Please, tell us about the enemy.

02:33.610 --> 02:35.050
We want to fight too.

02:38.010 --> 02:39.550
Our friend...

02:41.040 --> 02:43.870
She was killed back then.

02:46.190 --> 02:50.070
<i>Nobody could say whether this path was right.</i>

02:52.040 --> 02:56.940
<i>Only four days remained until Skylos' full assault.</i>

04:38.100 --> 04:39.500
It's Elder Rasha.

04:39.500 --> 04:41.720
I haven't seen her in a while.

04:41.720 --> 04:44.760
Didn't she only join the Council recently?

04:44.760 --> 04:47.020
Two years ago, I think.

04:47.020 --> 04:49.510
But look how unsteady she is.

04:52.050 --> 04:56.350
Put members of the SDF in charge of each squad's training.

04:56.350 --> 04:59.820
On the day of, they'll lead and protect their groups.

04:59.820 --> 05:02.270
What about members for the special operation?

05:02.270 --> 05:08.700
The biggest issue is that most Marked begin to lose thymia power in their late twenties.

05:09.090 --> 05:12.790
Our only option is to rely on the children.

05:12.790 --> 05:14.420
Children, huh.

05:15.580 --> 05:17.440
I'll start looking for volunteers.

05:20.830 --> 05:22.300
Elder Rasha.

05:22.810 --> 05:24.860
Are you well enough to be about?

05:24.860 --> 05:27.390
My health is the least of our worries.

05:30.740 --> 05:33.100
I believe you have the children training.

05:33.450 --> 05:35.150
Y-Yes.

05:36.770 --> 05:37.810
New Chieftain.

05:41.580 --> 05:45.190
It seems that they killed your sister.

05:47.130 --> 05:52.790
You must detest those outsiders. But you must never forget this—

05:53.300 --> 05:57.580
Tomorrow, the children might end up having to kill someone.

05:57.580 --> 06:00.040
Tomorrow, they might end up dying.

06:00.580 --> 06:03.880
And <i>you</i> are the one who will have decided that.

06:03.880 --> 06:09.460
Elder Rasha, Suou cares more about the children than anyone else.

06:09.460 --> 06:12.330
Kuchiba, what about you?

06:12.330 --> 06:16.480
You were with Taisha, and yet you were unable to protect her.

06:16.480 --> 06:19.640
Do you intend to fight for revenge?

06:19.640 --> 06:26.650
You don't have the ability to fight. It's the Marked children whose lives will be sacrificed.

06:26.650 --> 06:27.680
Kuchiba!

06:27.680 --> 06:32.310
The only answer you Elders could come up with was mass suicide!

06:32.310 --> 06:33.800
If you want to complain—

06:32.950 --> 06:33.800
Go ahead.

06:34.330 --> 06:35.950
Do as you wish.

06:36.300 --> 06:39.040
Either way, everything will soon be over.

06:39.510 --> 06:44.300
The cursed children of the whale will be saved at long last.

06:47.200 --> 06:48.340
Elder Rasha.

06:49.380 --> 06:52.010
If we do nothing, we are simply waiting for death.

06:52.610 --> 06:55.680
That is why we can't afford to stop here!

07:06.870 --> 07:07.950
Ouni.

07:09.310 --> 07:12.400
Were you selected to be a member of the Chieftain's plan?

07:14.720 --> 07:16.590
Isn't it a dangerous mission?

07:20.230 --> 07:24.030
I'm gonna get something to eat.
Jiki, come with me.

07:26.880 --> 07:31.710
<i>Ouni appeared out of nowhere in a corner of the residential area one day.</i>

07:32.880 --> 07:36.250
<i>Nobody had any idea who his parents were.</i>

07:36.250 --> 07:38.720
<i>He wasn't part of any group either.</i>

07:39.610 --> 07:41.810
That kid's always by himself.

07:41.810 --> 07:43.230
I think his name's Ouni.

07:43.540 --> 07:45.990
What a weirdo. Let's leave him alone.

07:48.850 --> 07:50.140
Hey, you.

07:51.480 --> 07:53.070
I'll let you be my underling.

07:55.640 --> 07:57.950
I'm saying I'll let you play with us!

07:57.950 --> 07:58.450
Wait!

08:02.020 --> 08:04.110
Why you...

08:10.130 --> 08:10.670
Take this!

08:14.480 --> 08:16.550
Fighting is against the rules.

08:16.550 --> 08:20.360
He's the one who punched my face!

08:20.360 --> 08:22.020
I let him be my underling...

08:22.020 --> 08:22.940
But he didn't—

08:22.940 --> 08:25.980
I'm going to have you spend some time together in the bowels.

08:26.450 --> 08:28.460
Be sure to talk it out.

08:29.940 --> 08:32.860
Dammit, I don't wanna be here!

08:32.860 --> 08:34.390
Let me out!

08:34.390 --> 08:36.390
You want to get out that bad?

08:36.390 --> 08:38.360
In here is no different from outside.

08:38.360 --> 08:42.750
Of course it's different! You don't care about being in a tiny place like this?

08:43.230 --> 08:44.710
This island is tiny too.

08:46.730 --> 08:50.570
We're surrounded by sand and can't move freely.

08:50.570 --> 08:53.750
We'll just grow up and then die trapped here.

08:53.750 --> 08:54.880
They're the same.

08:56.860 --> 08:59.390
Th-Then you just have to leave!

08:59.740 --> 09:03.520
You scaredy scaredy scaredy-cat!
Just get off the island if you don't like it!

09:05.630 --> 09:09.020
And if you can't do it yourself, then <i>I'll</i> take you!

09:19.370 --> 09:21.040
Oh, right.

09:21.040 --> 09:23.540
Now you've definitely gotta be my underling.

09:24.740 --> 09:29.590
I mean, my minion! But I guess that's the same thing.

09:29.590 --> 09:30.540
I know!

09:31.000 --> 09:32.250
Be my comrade.

09:32.250 --> 09:35.880
If you do, I'll take you outside.

09:40.600 --> 09:42.640
Hey, time's up.

09:43.430 --> 09:47.210
Doesn't it suck in the bowels?
Be more careful unless you—

09:49.450 --> 09:51.820
It's not so bad once in a while, right?

10:08.990 --> 10:11.620
Nibi. What will you do?

10:12.140 --> 10:13.320
Will you fight?

10:13.320 --> 10:16.470
I haven't given up on getting to the outside world.

10:19.240 --> 10:23.610
I'll beat up anyone in my way and take you out there.

10:25.890 --> 10:28.390
Don't forget that I used to be the leader.

10:28.390 --> 10:29.310
I haven't.

10:29.310 --> 10:34.010
I still consider myself that, in fact.
Besides, I'm a year older than you.

10:34.010 --> 10:35.320
Don't laugh!

10:36.890 --> 10:38.240
Those days were fun.

10:46.490 --> 10:50.000
But now I'll never be able to see them again!

10:54.610 --> 10:55.250
Don't cry.

10:55.250 --> 10:56.790
I can't!

10:57.620 --> 11:01.040
I'm not strong like you.

11:02.340 --> 11:03.990
You're amazing.

11:04.770 --> 11:08.760
I've never seen you cry even once.

11:11.120 --> 11:15.720
Ouni... I've always been kind of scared.

11:16.610 --> 11:18.980
I have no idea how you see the world.

11:19.570 --> 11:24.660
I'm worried that one day you'll leave us behind and disappear somewhere on your own.

11:27.270 --> 11:28.200
I'm not going anywhere.

11:31.310 --> 11:34.670
<i>I wish you'd look at me when you say that, Ouni.</i>

11:45.270 --> 11:46.320
Chakuro.

11:52.340 --> 11:53.190
Lykos.

11:53.580 --> 11:55.840
You changed? It looks nice.

11:59.990 --> 12:01.360
Here.

12:01.860 --> 12:07.730
Your clothes are dirty and ripped up...
so I remade some of the things I received into this.

12:07.730 --> 12:09.700
You made this for me?

12:11.670 --> 12:13.040
Don't wear it if you don't want to.

12:13.040 --> 12:14.760
Hey, Lykos?

12:21.550 --> 12:22.550
<i>I knew it...</i>

12:25.020 --> 12:27.990
<i>Feelings just get in the way...</i>

12:31.760 --> 12:33.230
What're you doing?

12:33.230 --> 12:34.970
Getting shand together.

12:34.970 --> 12:37.190
Tomorrow's the Sand Returning Day.

12:41.180 --> 12:44.320
The eastern barricade is eighty percent complete.

12:44.630 --> 12:47.050
The western one's behind schedule, but...

12:47.810 --> 12:48.810
Suou?

12:49.540 --> 12:50.710
It's probably impossible.

12:50.710 --> 12:54.540
No, if we direct everyone free to help, then the western Sand Returning—

12:52.100 --> 12:52.910
The Sand Returning.

12:55.680 --> 12:59.500
You really think we have time to play in the sand when we know they're coming?

12:59.810 --> 13:03.310
The kids were all looking forward to it...

13:03.310 --> 13:05.010
But we really can't.

13:05.010 --> 13:07.390
Anyway, we have the rally to worry about tomorrow.

13:07.710 --> 13:09.950
We need to unite everyone.

13:09.950 --> 13:12.120
That one's on you, Chieftain.

13:19.580 --> 13:24.820
Be sure to confirm your position and duties and prepare for all eventualities.

13:24.820 --> 13:27.500
That concludes the briefing for tomorrow.

13:31.140 --> 13:33.200
We will likely face horror.

13:33.540 --> 13:35.910
We will likely face sorrow.

13:35.910 --> 13:43.340
Even so, our hearts will always be connected through the sky above and the Sand Ocean below.

13:44.180 --> 13:50.050
If you feel as though you'll be crushed by fear and despair, just remember this prayer.

13:51.540 --> 13:56.520
All of the lives connecting you are forever in your hearts.

13:56.520 --> 13:57.730
Master Suou!

14:00.730 --> 14:02.760
He gets a passing grade this time.

14:02.760 --> 14:03.940
That was wonderful.

14:10.610 --> 14:11.460
Up there!

14:12.270 --> 14:17.040
The workshop has shed blood, sweat, and tears over the last year preparing this masterpiece for today.

14:17.540 --> 14:20.500
It's an autonomous sand-throwing machine. We call it:

14:20.500 --> 14:22.840
The Autonomous Sand-Throwing Machine!

14:22.840 --> 14:24.210
That's the same thing.

14:25.880 --> 14:26.970
Do you think...

14:27.940 --> 14:31.400
that I won't get angry no matter what you do to me?

14:31.910 --> 14:32.890
Hey!

14:32.890 --> 14:36.760
Nezu! Rou! Chakuro! Get down here this instant!

14:33.620 --> 14:35.210
He's madder than I expected.

14:35.210 --> 14:38.900
We'll be fine! Just run, he's got no stamina.

14:36.760 --> 14:38.900
Even <i>I</i> get angry, you know!

14:38.900 --> 14:39.350
Push.

14:39.350 --> 14:40.190
Get back here!

14:41.940 --> 14:44.020
Master Suou threw sand!

14:44.020 --> 14:44.940
It's Sand Returning!

14:45.940 --> 14:48.320
H-Hey! Suou, stop them!

14:50.990 --> 14:52.200
Not today!

14:53.240 --> 14:58.320
<i>The Sand Returning is an annual festival where people throw sand at each other regardless of status.</i>

14:58.320 --> 15:03.880
<i>Every person on the Mud Whale partakes in the sand throwing contest until the sun sets.</i>

15:04.800 --> 15:08.130
<i>There is also one more meaning behind the Sand Returning.</i>

15:09.250 --> 15:15.560
<i>The souls that have melded into the sand pass
out of it into the air and return to us once again.</i>

15:17.690 --> 15:18.740
Sami.

15:20.180 --> 15:24.980
<i>I'm sorry for smiling so shortly after your death.</i>

15:25.940 --> 15:28.150
<i>But I haven't forgotten about you once.</i>

15:29.080 --> 15:31.210
<i>I'll always remember you.</i>

15:42.470 --> 15:44.290
<i>Please watch over me.</i>

16:05.850 --> 16:07.860
What is it, Sienna?

16:10.410 --> 16:11.110
Dear...

16:16.050 --> 16:19.120
I'll be participating in the battle too.

16:19.650 --> 16:21.830
I also have an order from the Council.

16:22.680 --> 16:24.210
Prepare to take your own life.

16:25.090 --> 16:27.160
You wouldn't want to leave a displeasing corpse.

16:29.900 --> 16:32.510
Is your heart incapable of feeling?

16:34.070 --> 16:37.300
Do you only care about whether your wife dies in an ugly fashion?

16:39.980 --> 16:44.370
Emotions aren't something you can touch or see.

16:44.370 --> 16:48.810
Why are you so concerned with something nobody can ever understand?

17:20.950 --> 17:21.680
Neri!

17:22.240 --> 17:24.310
I'm so glad you're okay!

17:24.900 --> 17:26.820
After all that with Falaina, why—

17:27.520 --> 17:28.310
You're not Neri.

17:29.790 --> 17:32.870
Who are you? Where's Neri?

17:32.870 --> 17:37.820
She went back to Mama's belly to heal Mama's wounds.

17:38.180 --> 17:40.160
Mama? Who's tha—

17:40.160 --> 17:44.000
So you can actually hear my voice! Thank goodness.

17:44.830 --> 17:47.460
It's been so long since I talked to someone.

17:48.370 --> 17:52.280
I'm actually Neri's twin sister.

17:52.280 --> 17:53.590
Call me Ema.

17:54.390 --> 17:55.200
Ema?

17:55.200 --> 17:57.380
That's right, Archivist.

17:58.340 --> 18:00.680
Hey, make me a promise!

18:01.900 --> 18:03.810
Wh-What? A promise?

18:05.000 --> 18:10.460
Promise that you'll protect this island, like you said underground.

18:10.460 --> 18:15.960
Live here with everyone forever and ever! Promise!

18:17.140 --> 18:22.280
If you come back alive, I'll tell you all of Falaina's secrets.

18:22.690 --> 18:26.560
You mean the history of the
Mud Whale? You know about it?

18:46.890 --> 18:49.520
Ema! Just what are you and Neri?

18:49.920 --> 18:52.020
What are you trying to tell me?!

19:02.760 --> 19:06.790
<i>93 Sand Era. Seventeenth day of the seventh month.</i>

19:07.250 --> 19:11.790
<i>Before sunrise, a blinding fog of sand rolled in.</i>

19:13.200 --> 19:19.780
<i>Soon after, the sea bore a sandstorm, severely limiting our range of vision.</i>

19:20.430 --> 19:23.800
The Mud Whale will soon be under siege.

19:24.320 --> 19:29.390
Our highest priority is to protect our own lives from the enemy.

19:30.120 --> 19:35.440
The objective is to stall for time, repel the attack, and survive.

19:36.230 --> 19:37.830
Then there is our secondary mission.

19:39.670 --> 19:45.870
While we are defending ourselves,
you will infiltrate the enemy battleship.

19:45.870 --> 19:51.330
You will locate and destroy the nous Skylos, sinking their ship.

19:51.820 --> 19:54.960
This will be a highly dangerous mission.

19:54.960 --> 19:59.460
That is why only the strongest thymia users have been assigned.

20:00.150 --> 20:02.720
I braided these protection charms myself.

20:03.210 --> 20:08.140
Normally they would be worn to remain safe on expeditions, but I'd like everyone to have one.

20:10.700 --> 20:12.260
Please come back safely.

20:12.260 --> 20:14.120
I will, Master Suou.

20:14.120 --> 20:16.110
Good girl! Nice answer.

20:16.440 --> 20:17.380
Thanks.

20:17.380 --> 20:18.830
Be careful.

20:18.830 --> 20:19.990
Keep it.

20:20.780 --> 20:21.340
But...

20:21.340 --> 20:22.240
Just back off.

20:23.490 --> 20:25.740
Don't say that. I'll tie it.

20:26.600 --> 20:32.770
I'm the SDF Third Squad's leader, Tokusa. I'm in charge of this special op.

20:32.770 --> 20:36.630
We're all in this together, so let's get along, Ouni.

20:37.100 --> 20:39.190
I'm counting on you, Tokusa.

20:39.190 --> 20:41.130
Don't be like that, Master Suou.

20:41.130 --> 20:45.080
Aren't we friends? Have a little faith!

20:45.080 --> 20:46.220
Sure...

20:47.420 --> 20:48.300
Lykos.

20:49.700 --> 20:52.180
You're a member of the Mud Whale now.

20:52.180 --> 20:57.080
Value your own life, and come back home safe and sound.

20:57.080 --> 20:57.770
Okay.

20:57.770 --> 20:59.990
Good girl. Nice answer.

20:59.990 --> 21:03.230
Chakuro, I want you to be especially careful when you see the nous—

21:03.230 --> 21:05.160
Don't worry, Suou.

21:06.430 --> 21:07.530
Just leave it to us.

21:09.780 --> 21:12.540
Thank you, Chakuro.

21:18.500 --> 21:22.380
When you finish loading your supplies,
get in your boats and go on standby!

21:27.450 --> 21:28.510
I'm coming too!

21:28.850 --> 21:31.210
Nibi, you weren't chosen.

21:31.210 --> 21:32.640
Stay here and protect the others.

21:32.640 --> 21:35.270
No way. I've had enough of being left behind!

21:37.730 --> 21:40.640
Nibi, while I appreciate your enthusiasm—

21:40.640 --> 21:42.980
Shut up! This has nothing to do with the damn SDF!

21:42.980 --> 21:44.560
Calm down!

21:46.870 --> 21:49.510
Hey, don't you hear something?

21:50.890 --> 21:53.210
There's something besides the sandstorm.

21:53.210 --> 21:54.160
What?

22:00.850 --> 22:01.880
They're here.

22:01.880 --> 22:03.840
The enemy is right in front of us!
